g its derivative and applying the initial condition."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"بالتكامل نحصل على $y=6x^2+C$.","En":"Integration gives $y=6x^2+C$."},{"Ar":"باستخدام $y(0)=7$ يكون الحل $y=6x^2+7$؛ ثم نعوض المدخل المطلوب.","En":"Using $y(0)=7$, the solution is $y=6x^2+7$; then evaluate the requested input."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$223$","En":"$223$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تهمل الشرط الابتدائي.","En":"Do not omit the initial condition."},"FormulaLatex":"y(x)=y(0)+\\int_0^x g(t)\\,dt","Substitution":{"Ar":"$y(6)=6(6)^2+7=223$","En":"$y(6)=6(6)^2+7=223$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$(6x^2+7)'=12x,\\quad y(0)=7$","En":"$(6x^2+7)'=12x,\\quad y(0)=7$"}},"Distractors":[{"ErrorType":"misconception","Reason":{"Ar":"الجزء المتغير يساوي $216$؛ اختيار $226$ يتطلب ثابت تكامل $10$ بدلاً من $7$، فلا يحقق الشرط الابتدائي.","En":"The variable part is $216$; choice $226$ requires integration constant $10$ instead of $7$, violating the initial condition."},"Order":1},{"ErrorType":"misconception","Reason":{"Ar":"الجزء المتغير يساوي $216$؛ اختيار $221$ يتطلب ثابت تكامل $5$ بدلاً من $7$، فلا يحقق الشرط الابتدائي.","En":"The variable part is $216$; choice $221$ requires integration constant $5$ instead of $7$, violating the initial condition."},"Order":2},{"ErrorType":"","Reason":null,"Order":3},{"ErrorType":"misconception","Reason":{"Ar":"الجزء المتغير يساوي $216$؛ اختيار $224$ يتطلب ثابت تكامل $8$ بدلاً من $7$، فلا يحقق الشرط الابتدائي.","En":"The variable part is $216$; choice $224$ requires integration constant $8$ instead of $7$, violating the initial condition."},"Order":4}]}$mw$,$mw$نستعيد الدالة بتكامل مشتقتها واستعمال الشرط الابتدائي.

$y(x)=y(0)+\int_0^x g(t)\,dt$

1. بالتكامل نحصل على $y=6x^2+C$.

2. باستخدام $y(0)=7$ يكون الحل $y=6x^2+7$؛ ثم نعوض المدخل المطلوب.

$y(6)=6(6)^2+7=223$

$223$ بلا وحدة قياس

$(6x^2+7)'=12x,\quad y(0)=7$

لا تهمل الشرط الابتدائي.$mw$,$mw$Recover the function by integrating its derivative and applying the initial condition.

$y(x)=y(0)+\int_0^x g(t)\,dt$

1. Integration gives $y=6x^2+C$.

2. Using $y(0)=7$, the solution is $y=6x^2+7$; then evaluate the requested input.

$y(6)=6(6)^2+7=223$

$223$ Dimensionless

$(6x^2+7)'=12x,\quad y(0)=7$

Do not omit the initial condition.$mw$),
(592,386,$mw$EEA6010A94DC360A4561BC148B43DF92B1472C8356CF23A04C0508A42C5BD9DB$mw$,$mw$9b56a9d8d669bb69233dcde4157c9de1$mw$,$mw$$mw$,$mw${"Id":386,"StageId":4,"CategoryId":36,"Points":15,"TitleAr":"أوجد نهاية \\(a_n=\\frac{6}{n+1}\\) عندما \\(n\\to\\infty\\).","TitleEn":"Find limit of \\(a_n=\\frac{6}{n+1}\\) as n tends to infinity.","QuestionTextAr":"أوجد نهاية \\(a_n=\\frac{6}{n+1}\\) عندما \\(n\\to\\infty\\).","QuestionTextEn":"Find limit of \\(a_n=\\frac{6}{n+1}\\) as n tends to infinity.","DetailedSolutionAr":"القانون المستخدم: الكسر ذو البسط الثابت والمقام الذي يزداد إلى ما لا نهاية يتقارب إلى الصفر. للمتتالية aₙ = 6/(n+1)، لأي ε > 0 نختار n أكبر من 6/ε، عندها 0 < 6/(n+1) < ε. إذن lim(aₙ) عندما n → ∞ يساوي 0.","DetailedSolutionEn":"Rule used: A constant divided by a denominator increasing without bound has limit zero. For aₙ = 6/(n+1), given any ε > 0 choose n > 6/ε. Then 0 < 6/(n+1) < ε, proving lim(n→∞) aₙ = 0.","YoutubeSolutionUrl":null,"EditorialDetailsJson":null,"Options":[{"Id":1533,"Order":1,"LatexCode":"1","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":1534,"Order":2,"LatexCode":"6","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":1535,"Order":3,"LatexCode":"+\\infty","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":1536,"Order":4,"LatexCode":"0","IsCorrect":true}]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"Hints":[{"Ar":"راقب سلوك الحد مع ازدياد الرتبة.","En":"Examine term behavior as the index increases."},{"Ar":"قارن الكسر بكمية تؤول للصفر.","En":"Compare with a quantity tending to zero."}],"Title":{"Ar":"أوجد نهاية \\(a_n=\\frac{6}{n+1}\\) عندما \\(n\\to\\infty\\).","En":"Find limit of \\(a_n=\\frac{6}{n+1}\\) as n tends to infinity."},"Points":15,"Options":[{"Reason":{"Ar":"القيمة $1$ موجبة ثابتة، بينما يمكن جعل الحد أصغر من أي مقدار موجب بزيادة $n$.","En":"Choice $1$ is a fixed positive value, whereas increasing $n$ makes the term smaller than any positive amount."},"ErrorType":"misconception","IsCorrect":false,"LatexCode":"1"},{"Reason":{"Ar":"القيمة $6$ موجبة ثابتة، بينما يمكن جعل الحد أصغر من أي مقدار موجب بزيادة $n$.","En":"Choice $6$ is a fixed positive value, whereas increasing $n$ makes the term smaller than any positive amount."},"ErrorType":"misconception","IsCorrect":false,"LatexCode":"6"},{"Reason":{"Ar":"خلط نمو المقام أو الأس مع نمو الحد نفسه؛ الحد يتناقص.","En":"Confuses growth of the denominator or exponent with growth of the term; the term decreases."},"ErrorType":"misconception","IsCorrect":false,"LatexCode":"+\\infty"},{"Reason":null,"ErrorType":"","IsCorrect":true,"LatexCode":"0"}],"StageId":4,"Question":{"Ar":"أوجد نهاية \\(a_n=\\frac{6}{n+1}\\) عندما \\(n\\to\\infty\\).","En":"Find limit of \\(a_n=\\frac{6}{n+1}\\) as n tends to infinity."},"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"البسط ثابت والمقام يزداد بلا حد.","En":"A fixed numerator is divided by an unbounded denominator."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"البسط $6$ ثابت، والمقام يزداد بلا حد.","En":"The numerator $6$ is fixed and the denominator grows without bound."},{"Ar":"لـ $n\\ge1$، لدينا $0<\\frac{6}{n+1}\\le\\frac{6}n$؛ نطبق مبرهنة الحصر.","En":"For $n\\ge1$, $0<\\frac{6}{n+1}\\le\\frac{6}n$; apply the squeeze theorem."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$0$","En":"$0$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تخلط الحد الأول بالنهاية.","En":"Do not confuse the first term with the limit."},"FormulaLatex":"\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac{c}{n+1}=0\\quad(c>0)","Substitution":{"Ar":"$\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac{6}{n+1}=0$","En":"$\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac{6}{n+1}=0$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"لكل $\\varepsilon>0$، يكفي $n>6/\\varepsilon$.","En":"For every $\\varepsilon>0$, $n>6/\\varepsilon$ suffices."}},"TrackIds":[13,20],"CategoryId":36,"PrimarySkillId":72,"DifficultyLevel":1,"SecondarySkillIds":[]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"DifficultyLevel":1,"Hints":[{"Ar":"راقب سلوك الحد مع ازدياد الرتبة.","En":"Examine term behavior as the index increases."},{"Ar":"قارن الكسر بكمية تؤول للصفر.","En":"Compare with a quantity tending to zero."}],"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"البسط ثابت والمقام يزداد بلا حد.","En":"A fixed numerator is divided by an unbounded denominator."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"البسط $6$ ثابت، والمقام يزداد بلا حد.","En":"The numerator $6$ is fixed and the denominator grows without bound."},{"Ar":"لـ $n\\ge1$، لدينا $0<\\frac{6}{n+1}\\le\\frac{6}n$؛ نطبق مبرهنة الحصر.","En":"For $n\\ge1$, $0<\\frac{6}{n+1}\\le\\frac{6}n$; apply the squeeze theorem."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$0$","En":"$0$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تخلط الحد الأول بالنهاية.","En":"Do not confuse the first term with the limit."},"FormulaLatex":"\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac{c}{n+1}=0\\quad(c>0)","Substitution":{"Ar":"$\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac{6}{n+1}=0$","En":"$\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac{6}{n+1}=0$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"لكل $\\varepsilon>0$، يكفي $n>6/\\varepsilon$.","En":"For every $\\varepsilon>0$, $n>6/\\varepsilon$ suffices."}},"Distractors":[{"ErrorType":"misconception","Reason":{"Ar":"القيمة $1$ موجبة ثابتة، بينما يمكن جعل الحد أصغر من أي مقدار موجب بزيادة $n$.","En":"Choice $1$ is a fixed positive value, whereas increasing $n$ makes the term smaller than any positive amount."},"Order":1},{"ErrorType":"misconception","Reason":{"Ar":"القيمة $6$ موجبة ثابتة، بينما يمكن جعل الحد أصغر من أي مقدار موجب بزيادة $n$.","En":"Choice $6$ is a fixed positive value, whereas increasing $n$ makes the term smaller than any positive amount."},"Order":2},{"ErrorType":"misconception","Reason":{"Ar":"خلط نمو المقام أو الأس مع نمو الحد نفسه؛ الحد يتناقص.","En":"Confuses growth of the denominator or exponent with growth of the term; the term decreases."},"Order":3},{"ErrorType":"","Reason":null,"Order":4}]}$mw$,$mw$البسط ثابت والمقام يزداد بلا حد.

$\lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{c}{n+1}=0\quad(c>0)$

1. البسط $6$ ثابت، والمقام يزداد بلا حد.

2. لـ $n\ge1$، لدينا $0<\frac{6}{n+1}\le\frac{6}n$؛ نطبق مبرهنة الحصر.

$\lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{6}{n+1}=0$

$0$ بلا وحدة قياس

لكل $\varepsilon>0$، يكفي $n>6/\varepsilon$.

لا تخلط الحد الأول بالنهاية.$mw$,$mw$A fixed numerator is divided by an unbounded denominator.

$\lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{c}{n+1}=0\quad(c>0)$

1. The numerator $6$ is fixed and the denominator grows without bound.

2. For $n\ge1$, $0<\frac{6}{n+1}\le\frac{6}n$; apply the squeeze theorem.

$\lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{6}{n+1}=0$

$0$ Dimensionless

For every $\varepsilon>0$, $n>6/\varepsilon$ suffices.

Do not confuse the first term with the limit.$mw$),
